{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rey2MAHwAEYJ6ZeromJXdh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# .anchor/ — Anchor R&D per-project store\n2\t\n3\tThis directory is created and managed by Anchor's R&D control surface. Each\n4\tregistered project gets an isolated namespace at:\n5\t\n6\t    .anchor/projects/<project-id>/\n7\t        research/      planning/      build/      deliverables/      jobs/\n8\t\n9\tMultiple projects may share one folder; each has its own `<project-id>` subtree,\n10\tso their stores never collide.\n11\t\n12\t## Tracking policy (C9 git-trackable vs C10 no-leak)\n13\t\n14\t- **Tracked (C9):** small JSON *pointer-records* that index efforts/versions —\n15\t  these are committed so effort history is durable across restarts.\n16\t- **Ignored (C10):** raw job logs, large generated artifacts (PDF), and any\n17\t  `raw/` payloads that could carry absolute paths, tokens, or personal data.\n18\t  The distribution build (Wave 8) additionally scans for and refuses to ship\n19\t  anything under `.anchor/`.\n20\t\n21\tSee the sibling `.gitignore` for the exact rules.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fceae531-e83d-498c-ba18-66031f19154b","uuid":"339ce61b-a299-4ecb-b759-c43014e40c4e","timestamp":"2026-06-23T22:10:32.448Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\john\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\pytest-of-john\\pytest-2148\\test_select_existing_project_b0\\registered\\.anchor\\README","content":"# .anchor/ — Anchor R&D per-project store\n\nThis directory is created and managed by Anchor's R&D control surface. Each\nregistered project gets an isolated namespace at:\n\n    .anchor/projects/<project-id>/\n        research/      planning/      build/      deliverables/      jobs/\n\nMultiple projects may share one folder; each has its own `<project-id>` subtree,\nso their stores never collide.\n\n## Tracking policy (C9 git-trackable vs C10 no-leak)\n\n- **Tracked (C9):** small JSON *pointer-records* that index efforts/versions —\n  these are committed so effort history is durable across restarts.\n- **Ignored (C10):** raw job logs, large generated artifacts (PDF), and any\n  `raw/` payloads that could carry absolute paths, tokens, or personal data.\n  The distribution build (Wave 8) additionally scans for and refuses to ship\n  anything under `.anchor/`.\n\nSee the sibling `.gitignore` for the exact rules.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
